    <div class="eyebrow">The ELSEWHERE guide / 02</div>
    <h1>Best Travel Apps for Europe</h1>
    <p class="intro">One weekend. Endless possibilities. Whether you're catching a train to Paris or booking a last-minute flight to Barcelona, the right travel apps can make exploring Europe easier.</p>

    <h2>Europe is yours to explore.</h2>
    <p>One of the most exciting parts of studying abroad is the opportunity to experience different countries, cultures, and cities. But planning transportation can get complicated. Here's how to choose useful travel apps for your next adventure.</p>

    <div class="feature">
      <span class="tag">Trains</span>
      <h3>01. Trainline — Make train travel easier</h3>
      <p>Trainline helps travelers search and book train journeys across supported European rail networks. It's especially helpful when comparing departure times, routes, and ticket options.</p>
      <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Weekend rail trips, exploring neighboring cities, and comparing train schedules.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature">
      <span class="tag">Flights</span>
      <h3>02. Ryanair — Explore budget flight options</h3>
      <p>Ryanair operates flights between many European destinations. Its app allows travelers to search flights, manage bookings, and access travel information.</p>
      <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Students comparing low-cost flights between European cities. Remember to check baggage restrictions and airport transfers.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature">
      <span class="tag">Airlines</span>
      <h3>03. Lufthansa — Manage longer journeys</h3>
      <p>The Lufthansa app helps passengers manage eligible flight bookings, access boarding passes, and receive journey updates.</p>
      <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Students booking connecting flights or traveling between their home country and their study-abroad destination.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature">
      <span class="tag">Compare routes</span>
      <h3>04. Omio — Compare more than one way to travel</h3>
      <p>Omio brings different transportation options together, helping travelers evaluate whether a train, bus, or flight makes the most sense for a particular journey.</p>
      <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Comparing costs and journey times before choosing a route.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="feature">
      <span class="tag">Local rides</span>
      <h3>05. FreeNow — Get around the city</h3>
      <p>FreeNow offers taxi and other mobility booking services in participating European cities. Availability depends on your destination.</p>
      <p><strong>Best for:</strong> Getting to your accommodation or arranging a ride when public transportation isn't convenient.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="tip">
      <div class="eyebrow">Travel smarter</div>
      <h2>The cheapest ticket isn't always the cheapest trip.</h2>
      <p>Before booking, calculate the full cost of your journey. A low-cost flight might require a long airport transfer, additional baggage fees, or an overnight stay. Compare total expenses, departure times, and how much time you'll actually have to explore.</p>
    </div>

    <h2>Make every weekend count.</h2>
    <p>Build a travel routine that works around your classes. Research transportation early, save your confirmations, and leave room for unexpected discoveries.</p>
